{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Virtual Destructor in Algorithm Hierarchies.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Virtual Destructor in Algorithm Hierarchies.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"virtual destructor in algorithm hierarchies virtual destructor in algorithm hierarchies","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Virtual Destructor in Algorithm Hierarchies.md","fileName":"Virtual Destructor in Algorithm Hierarchies.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Virtual Destructor in Algorithm Hierarchies","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-14 22:06\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[C++ Clustering Object Model]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["C++ Clustering Object Model","dataclusteringincplusplus.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Virtual Destructor in Algorithm Hierarchies.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Virtual Destructor in Algorithm Hierarchies.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"virtual destructor in algorithm hierarchies virtual destructor in algorithm hierarchies","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Virtual Destructor in Algorithm Hierarchies.md","fileName":"Virtual Destructor in Algorithm Hierarchies.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Virtual Destructor in Algorithm Hierarchies","heading":"Virtual Destructor in Algorithm Hierarchies","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A virtual destructor ensures that deleting an object through a base pointer invokes the derived destructor before the base destructor. ClusLib gives base classes such as Algorithm, Distance, Cluster, Schema, and Node virtual destructors when they participate in runtime polymorphism.\n\nWithout this rule, derived resources may not be released and behavior is undefined. Declaring the destructor virtual documents that the class is intended as a polymorphic boundary even when the base itself owns little state.","tags":["baby"],"links":["C++ Clustering Object Model","dataclusteringincplusplus.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Virtual Destructor in Algorithm Hierarchies.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Virtual Destructor in Algorithm Hierarchies.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"virtual destructor in algorithm hierarchies virtual destructor in algorithm hierarchies","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Virtual Destructor in Algorithm Hierarchies.md","fileName":"Virtual Destructor in Algorithm Hierarchies.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Virtual Destructor in Algorithm Hierarchies","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[dataclusteringincplusplus.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["C++ Clustering Object Model","dataclusteringincplusplus.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}